  "IN",
  "MACHINE: every DONE item points at an existing declaration \u00b7\n         dependencies satisfied by the ordering \u00b7\n         the slice is within the comprehension ceiling.\nHUMAN:   Tony approves the grouping \u2014 what is in, what is deferred,\n         and why this cut rather than another.",
  "NOT A SCHEDULE.\ntime may be attached\nlater, or never.\n\nMVP / v1 / v1.2 are\nORDERED, not scheduled.\nconflating the two turns\na grouping decision into\na deadline argument.",
  "OUT",
  "OUT\nthe DONE\ncondition",
  "PRODUCT rung \u00b7 function 4 \u00b7 interviewed 2026-08-03\na release is a GROUPING, not a time axis. the DONE condition is assembled from upstream declarations, never authored at the end.",
  "RED \u2014 cost, or a route that leaves the stage / blocks it",
  "Slice a release \u00b7 Set the goal \u2014 stage flow",
  "THE CEILING IS THE UNUSUAL ONE.\nalmost everything sizes a release by what is READY \u2014\na bound from the producing side. this is a bound from\nthe RECEIVING side: a release can be too big even when\neverything in it is finished.\n\nit is why 'we shipped everything we had' is a real\nfailure mode and not a joke.",
  "THE GROUPING",
  "TWO ORPHANS RESOLVED WITHOUT NEW FUNCTIONS.\n'user testing passed' and 'documentation is\ncomplete' had no upstream declaration when\nthis started. user testing turned out to be a\nproof LAYER nobody had listed; documentation\nturned out to be DERIVED rather than declared.",
  "USER COMPREHENSION\nCEILING\n\nhow much change can be\nabsorbed AT ONCE.\ncaps the size.",
  "Walk the upstream declarations",
  "What actually decides the grouping",
  "What arrives",
  "five factors, and lumping them together is the mistake \u2014 they act on\nthe grouping in three different ways.",
  "if it does not, it cannot be checked \u2014 so it passes by ASSERTION.\nthat is the unqualified-risk failure in another costume: it looks\nhandled because it is written down.\n  fix it one of two ways: remove the item, or go and get the\n  declaration made upstream. never leave it unbacked.",
  "met the feature spec          <-  the contract\nmet the product spec          <-  the idea brief\ngoal of the function met      <-  the goal set here\nlooks EXACTLY like design     <-  design, approved before build\ntests pass                    <-  every proof layer declared by\n                                  Decide what proves it \u2014\n                                  INCLUDING user testing\ndocumentation complete        <-  DERIVED, not declared: every\n                                  declaration covered \u2014 feature,\n                                  product and problem specs, the\n                                  changes and fixes implemented,\n                                  the solution diagrams, and what\n                                  we ruled out",
  "risk arrives PRE-CHEWED.\ndo not re-assess it here.\n\na feature carrying a\nTEMPORARY countermeasure is\na different slicing\ncandidate from one carrying\na permanent fix.",
  "the DONE condition is ASSEMBLED, never authored. you do not write a\nwish list at the end \u2014 you walk what each rung already declared.",
  "the DONE condition is what /loop terminates on. a loop with a vague\nDONE condition is the one that runs forever \u2014 which is why the\nassembly rule above is load-bearing rather than tidy.",
  "the deferral is part of\nthe output, not the\nresidue. what did NOT\nmake the cut goes to\nWhat we ruled out.",
  "this is why the draft\nwas circular. 'specific\nenough to terminate a\nloop' is true EXACTLY\nwhen every item points\nat a declaration that\nexists.",
  "what is already built \u00b7 the framed and viability-tested candidates \u00b7\ntheir QUALIFIED risks with countermeasures attached \u00b7 and the record\nof what was already ruled out.",
